1
00:00:20,580 --> 00:00:21,410
you stop?

2
00:01:25,020 --> 00:01:26,420
Whoa!

3
00:01:28,160 --> 00:01:29,140
Whoa!

4
00:01:34,480 --> 00:01:35,880
Whoa!

5
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:46,080
Another round.

6
00:01:46,440 --> 00:01:48,040
Black Maria.

7
00:01:48,440 --> 00:01:50,200
Wait a minute.

8
00:01:50,900 --> 00:01:53,880
Don't you have a job to do a job?

9
00:01:54,140 --> 00:01:55,677
Why whatever could you mean?

10
00:01:55,760 --> 00:01:58,113
You're supposed to be looking for my son

11
00:01:59,760 --> 00:02:02,257
But wouldn't it be nicer
if I stayed here with

12
00:02:02,340 --> 00:02:06,040
you the other toby robo
may be insufferable,

13
00:02:06,200 --> 00:02:08,420
so I'll stay here and serve you.

14
00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:14,500
Fair enough, let's not
stand on ceremony today!

15
00:02:15,240 --> 00:02:18,460
So what do you say you having fun?

16
00:02:20,900 --> 00:02:23,560
Oh, you bet I am, my good man.

17
00:02:27,780 --> 00:02:32,080
For 20 long years, we've been haunted
by the ghosts of the Kozuki clan.

18
00:02:32,360 --> 00:02:34,217
But they've been vanquished at last.

19
00:02:34,300 --> 00:02:35,829
We have much to celebrate.

20
00:02:36,400 --> 00:02:39,106
Kanjuro deceived them
to the very last second.

21
00:02:39,580 --> 00:02:41,717
His grand performance has come to an end,

22
00:02:41,800 --> 00:02:44,317
so I imagine he'll be
joining us at any moment.

23
00:02:44,400 --> 00:02:47,477
The same goes for the
battleship captains who

24
00:02:47,560 --> 00:02:50,800
sent those Akazaya
samurai to a watery grave.

25
00:02:53,580 --> 00:02:54,815
Konjuro's impressive.

26
00:02:57,040 --> 00:03:01,337
To think I almost killed him by accident
in our battle all those years ago.

27
00:03:01,420 --> 00:03:04,557
But that doesn't mean Odin
trusted him with everything.

28
00:03:04,640 --> 00:03:08,337
Certainly not with the secrets he
discovered on his trip across the seas.

29
00:03:08,420 --> 00:03:12,680
But if Kanjuro wasn't told, then the
other samurai weren't told either?

30
00:03:13,660 --> 00:03:16,360
Still thinking about that? Of course.

31
00:03:17,020 --> 00:03:19,960
Odin knew the exact
location of Laugh Tale.

32
00:03:20,240 --> 00:03:22,960
The last island that Roger's crew reached.

33
00:03:26,800 --> 00:03:28,420
Who is this guy?

34
00:03:34,900 --> 00:03:36,760
Do pardon the intrusion.

35
00:03:37,100 --> 00:03:39,180
I must converse with Lord Orochi.

36
00:03:40,280 --> 00:03:42,300
Kandero, you made it.

37
00:03:42,680 --> 00:03:45,257
Is he one of us either way?

38
00:03:45,340 --> 00:03:47,046
He's trying to start a fight.

39
00:03:48,960 --> 00:03:50,417
The man works for order.

40
00:03:50,500 --> 00:03:51,540
See you, morons!

41
00:03:53,120 --> 00:03:54,580
Everyone stand down.

42
00:03:54,680 --> 00:03:56,209
Please forgive me my lord.

43
00:03:56,340 --> 00:03:57,257
I'm quite late.

44
00:03:57,340 --> 00:03:58,720
I Lost my way.

45
00:03:58,900 --> 00:04:01,020
This castle is much like a maze

46
00:04:04,020 --> 00:04:04,850
Furthermore,

47
00:04:04,933 --> 00:04:07,097
I was mistaken for an
enemy more than once and

48
00:04:07,180 --> 00:04:09,827
was forced to strike
down a number of guards.

49
00:04:10,260 --> 00:04:11,860
Again, my apologies.

50
00:04:12,680 --> 00:04:14,900
Oh, well, that is too bad for them.

51
00:04:16,100 --> 00:04:18,453
I see that you've brought a gift for me.

52
00:04:19,620 --> 00:04:23,140
As you requested, this
is Kozuki Momonosuke.

53
00:04:23,920 --> 00:04:26,500
Can you believe he's Odin's son?

54
00:04:29,220 --> 00:04:32,749
The boy cut the ropes and
attempted to escape along the way.

55
00:04:33,260 --> 00:04:35,201
Rest assured, he was disciplined.

56
00:04:35,380 --> 00:04:37,877
But do not fret, he still breathes.

57
00:04:37,960 --> 00:04:42,901
How could you do something so cruel to your
former lord and heir of the Kozuki clan?

58
00:04:43,900 --> 00:04:46,429
Quite a heartless one
you turned out to be.

59
00:04:46,940 --> 00:04:50,560
Now that my role is over, he's
naught but a lowly brat to me.

60
00:04:51,540 --> 00:04:54,740
I'm still surprised I
remember you from back then.

61
00:04:55,500 --> 00:04:58,676
It's hard to believe you
were one of the Akazaya Nine.

62
00:04:59,520 --> 00:05:00,897
Twenty years ago, was it?

63
00:05:00,980 --> 00:05:01,810
Our battle.

64
00:05:04,980 --> 00:05:08,620
And you, I remember our encounter as well.

65
00:05:09,420 --> 00:05:12,717
Some son of the great Kozuki
Oden you turned out to be.

66
00:05:12,800 --> 00:05:15,660
You haven't changed one bit, have you?

67
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:21,260
Quite a disappointment, isn't he?

68
00:05:21,700 --> 00:05:25,171
Seems that the only thing of
value that he has is his name.

69
00:05:25,700 --> 00:05:27,240
That poor child.

70
00:05:28,980 --> 00:05:32,620
Oh, how could you dare beat
this little boy black and blue?

71
00:05:35,900 --> 00:05:38,360
I'll toast to that, my good man.

72
00:05:38,960 --> 00:05:40,440
This one's for you.

73
00:05:40,640 --> 00:05:42,720
To conjure our sinister spine.

74
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:44,780
You do excellent work.

75
00:05:45,080 --> 00:05:46,256
Please, Lord Orochi.

76
00:05:46,460 --> 00:05:50,540
I do not deserve such praise,
for I bring you unfortunate news.

77
00:05:50,800 --> 00:05:54,797
The Straw Hat's appearance prevented
me from halting the Akasaya samurai.

78
00:05:54,880 --> 00:05:56,397
I have failed you.

79
00:05:56,480 --> 00:05:58,317
You should have called me Shula!

80
00:05:58,400 --> 00:05:59,230
That's not all.

81
00:05:59,313 --> 00:06:04,540
The rebel forces are advancing towards
Onigashima with the aid of 5,400 troops!

82
00:06:08,400 --> 00:06:10,120
You blasted fool!

83
00:06:10,540 --> 00:06:13,660
Your absolute incompetence
will be the death of me!

84
00:06:13,800 --> 00:06:15,320
I sincerely apologize.

85
00:06:15,980 --> 00:06:19,740
But you informed me of the
rendezvous point at Tokage Port!

86
00:06:20,020 --> 00:06:21,726
Why didn't you slay them all?

87
00:06:21,920 --> 00:06:23,957
Your excuse better be damn good!

88
00:06:24,040 --> 00:06:27,580
I'm loathe to admit it,
but Kin'emon outsmarted me.

89
00:06:28,140 --> 00:06:31,277
This is a shock since I have
known him for many years.

90
00:06:31,360 --> 00:06:34,654
Cunning is not a word I'd use
to describe his character.

91
00:06:34,900 --> 00:06:36,724
That sounds like a weak excuse.

92
00:06:36,840 --> 00:06:38,940
Now, Kanjuro, what do you know?

93
00:06:39,240 --> 00:06:41,077
Are the samurai on their way here?

94
00:06:41,160 --> 00:06:43,277
Is there something else
you're not telling me?

95
00:06:43,360 --> 00:06:46,160
No reason to lose your
head yet, Shogun Orochi.

96
00:06:47,840 --> 00:06:48,670
Fukurokuju.

97
00:06:48,753 --> 00:06:51,977
We haven't seen a single suspicious
ship at the dock thus far.

98
00:06:52,060 --> 00:06:55,317
Our only concern is that
the trio of battleships

99
00:06:55,400 --> 00:06:58,165
that we sent out earlier
have yet to come back.

100
00:06:58,800 --> 00:07:00,320
Not to alarm you,

101
00:07:00,440 --> 00:07:05,264
but there's a report that four pirates
have been sighted on the performance floor.

102
00:07:07,380 --> 00:07:08,820
Straw Hat Luffy.

103
00:07:12,560 --> 00:07:13,960
Pirate Hunter Zoro.

104
00:07:17,080 --> 00:07:18,800
Eustass Captain Kidd.

105
00:07:21,780 --> 00:07:23,337
Murder machine killer!

106
00:07:23,420 --> 00:07:26,597
It's quite likely that
their pirate crews are also

107
00:07:26,680 --> 00:07:29,177
in tow and have infiltrated
the island somehow?

108
00:07:29,260 --> 00:07:31,717
If you knew all that,
why didn't you tell me?

109
00:07:31,800 --> 00:07:35,237
Master, queen was supposed
to be handling the situation,

110
00:07:35,320 --> 00:07:38,677
so I thought it'd be better not to
interrupt the banquet with this nonsense!

111
00:07:38,760 --> 00:07:42,577
Sir, whether they're here or
not, we're more than prepared!

112
00:07:42,660 --> 00:07:43,740
Our entire...

113
00:07:44,380 --> 00:07:46,197
force is here on Onigashima.

114
00:07:46,280 --> 00:07:50,045
Whatever challenge is presented,
this is the safest place in the

115
00:07:53,280 --> 00:07:54,337
country at this moment.

116
00:07:54,420 --> 00:07:55,680
That's a good point.

117
00:07:56,140 --> 00:07:57,637
Have a drink, Orochi.

118
00:07:57,720 --> 00:07:59,660
Just relax. Let me pour

119
00:08:03,220 --> 00:08:04,050
you a cup.

120
00:08:04,133 --> 00:08:07,640
No, I don't want to hear
reassurances and platitudes.

121
00:08:08,020 --> 00:08:11,400
I won't be at ease until I
know Oh, the samurai are dead.

122
00:08:11,800 --> 00:08:13,140
They will locate me.

123
00:08:13,540 --> 00:08:15,100
I must have faith.

124
00:08:15,460 --> 00:08:17,695
You gotta find a way to survive, okay?

125
00:08:17,960 --> 00:08:20,800
Just hang on, and we'll come rescue you!

126
00:08:24,160 --> 00:08:25,960
I will persevere.

127
00:08:27,220 --> 00:08:29,940
Black Maria, give him to me.

128
00:08:30,300 --> 00:08:32,476
There's one thing we must not forget.

129
00:08:32,740 --> 00:08:35,916
This pathetic little brat
is still the enemy's leader.

130
00:08:37,680 --> 00:08:40,140
Don't prepare the stage for an execution!

131
00:08:40,940 --> 00:08:44,177
I'll bring an end to the Kozuki
bloodline in front of everyone!

132
00:08:44,260 --> 00:08:47,497
Then the samurai loyalty will
crumble right before my eyes!

133
00:08:47,580 --> 00:08:49,540
Then this will all be over!

134
00:08:53,880 --> 00:08:54,710
Luffy

135
00:08:55,680 --> 00:08:56,510
Everyone

136
00:08:58,540 --> 00:08:59,370
Father

137
00:09:05,740 --> 00:09:11,480
stupid cat, are you cara here of course
we just climbed up the waterfall?

138
00:09:16,440 --> 00:09:19,517
do you cara even know what day it is?

139
00:09:19,600 --> 00:09:22,417
why it's the night of the fire festival?

140
00:09:22,500 --> 00:09:28,340
obviously so we made it just in time; i'm
afraid the verdict is still out on that.

141
00:09:29,120 --> 00:09:30,238
We're almost there.

142
00:09:30,460 --> 00:09:33,437
We're on our way to the
northwest end of Onigashima.

143
00:09:33,520 --> 00:09:34,350
Sounds great.

144
00:09:34,433 --> 00:09:35,871
I'll see you gotta there.

145
00:09:36,040 --> 00:09:37,160
No, cat!

146
00:09:37,360 --> 00:09:39,500
We can't wait! Listen up!

147
00:09:39,800 --> 00:09:43,300
Kalik, I see our old friend
is as flippant as ever.

148
00:09:43,740 --> 00:09:46,517
Shall we place bets on if
he makes it there in time?

149
00:09:46,600 --> 00:09:47,980
Ka-ba-ba-ba!

150
00:09:48,380 --> 00:09:51,357
I haven't seen Kitty since
we were separated years ago.

151
00:09:51,440 --> 00:09:53,960
I imagine he got big like Dock did.

152
00:09:54,140 --> 00:09:55,200
I can't wait.

153
00:09:55,460 --> 00:09:57,040
This is a damn mess.

154
00:09:57,360 --> 00:09:58,900
Did he leave late or what?

155
00:09:59,120 --> 00:10:02,157
The raid is starting, so how the
hell is he going to make it in time?

156
00:10:02,240 --> 00:10:03,534
He's in a normal ship.

157
00:10:03,880 --> 00:10:07,660
The sea currents are far too
strong, except in the front.

158
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:08,840
In that case,

159
00:10:09,200 --> 00:10:13,057
I hope Kin'emon and Denjiro have reached
the back entrance without incident.

160
00:10:13,140 --> 00:10:13,970
Indeed.

161
00:10:14,280 --> 00:10:16,020
We're Lord Odin's retainers.

162
00:10:16,160 --> 00:10:18,557
We should avenge our
Lord's death together.

163
00:10:18,640 --> 00:10:21,940
Lord Momonosuke, we shall be there soon.

164
00:10:31,940 --> 00:10:33,780
Are they all right? Hmm?

165
00:10:34,780 --> 00:10:36,545
You gotta expect it otherwise.

166
00:10:36,820 --> 00:10:38,997
We were told that everyone
made it to the island,

167
00:10:39,080 --> 00:10:42,433
so it's safe to assume that
the raid is well in progress.

168
00:10:42,820 --> 00:10:45,996
They call that lonely little
isle Onigashima now, huh?

169
00:10:46,840 --> 00:10:51,157
Funny how you guys left long before I
did, but we made it at the same time.

170
00:10:51,240 --> 00:10:53,337
I asked you to send that message to Luffy,

171
00:10:53,420 --> 00:10:55,377
but I guess there is no
need for that in the end.

172
00:10:55,460 --> 00:10:56,290
You're gonna...

173
00:10:56,373 --> 00:10:57,203
Yeah!

174
00:10:57,440 --> 00:10:58,600
I almost forgot.

175
00:10:59,120 --> 00:11:01,179
No reason to hang on to this, then.

176
00:11:06,660 --> 00:11:09,954
I still find it hard to believe
you got involved, Marco.

177
00:11:10,540 --> 00:11:11,370
Really?

178
00:11:11,453 --> 00:11:12,864
I always did like Odin, though.

179
00:11:17,120 --> 00:11:22,061
This whole time I was ignorant to how bad
things had gotten around the land of Wano.

180
00:11:22,780 --> 00:11:25,545
Word rarely makes it past
the borders, if ever.

181
00:11:25,640 --> 00:11:27,177
So there's no way I would have known.

182
00:11:27,260 --> 00:11:29,580
Deserves much better than this.

183
00:11:30,440 --> 00:11:33,077
The damn Kaido is to
blame for its suffering.

184
00:11:33,160 --> 00:11:36,757
Hold on to those feelings and
use them when we get to the Isle.

185
00:11:36,840 --> 00:11:39,157
Let's not delay our vengeance any further.

186
00:11:39,240 --> 00:11:40,828
We should discuss the plan.

187
00:11:40,920 --> 00:11:42,567
The raid's already underway.

188
00:11:42,920 --> 00:11:45,377
How do we join them but
keep it on the down-low?

189
00:11:45,460 --> 00:11:47,166
I got something up my sleeve.

190
00:11:47,540 --> 00:11:49,305
You gotta just follow my lead.

191
00:11:53,380 --> 00:11:57,240
As planned, Denjiro leads his
samurai, the Southern Forces,

192
00:11:57,600 --> 00:11:59,424
towards the rear of the castle.

193
00:12:00,360 --> 00:12:02,300
This was not in the blueprints.

194
00:12:03,780 --> 00:12:04,680
Take cover!

195
00:12:08,020 --> 00:12:10,237
Toby Rope, this means trouble!

196
00:12:10,320 --> 00:12:13,202
Don't you dare come back
here until you find him.

197
00:12:14,100 --> 00:12:16,077
Perfect, now this I can work with.

198
00:12:16,160 --> 00:12:17,700
I know this idiot!

199
00:12:19,140 --> 00:12:21,660
Let me handle this who's there.

200
00:12:21,860 --> 00:12:26,320
Do not be alarmed Yoshiro
been a while hasn't it?

201
00:12:26,660 --> 00:12:27,980
Hey Sasaki.

202
00:12:28,340 --> 00:12:29,580
Hey, it is you.

203
00:12:29,760 --> 00:12:33,017
I was told you weren't coming
this year It's a surprise.

204
00:12:33,100 --> 00:12:35,617
So don't tell anyone
what's with the kid up.

205
00:12:35,700 --> 00:12:38,417
You look weird without
your pompadour I find

206
00:12:38,500 --> 00:12:40,897
it much stranger that
you're not at the feast.

207
00:12:40,980 --> 00:12:41,917
Yeah. Yeah Well,

208
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:44,097
I can't enjoy myself
to the commander's son

209
00:12:44,180 --> 00:12:47,160
turns up You wanna throw one back with me?

210
00:12:47,620 --> 00:12:49,700
I'd love to. Listen up!

211
00:12:49,860 --> 00:12:51,617
I'll catch up with you guys later!

212
00:12:51,700 --> 00:12:53,700
Head to the Skull Dome without me!

213
00:12:54,780 --> 00:12:59,251
Despite an unexpected obstacle and an
encounter with Sasaki of the Tobiropo,

214
00:12:59,920 --> 00:13:02,197
Kyoshiro quickly turns
the situation around.

215
00:13:02,280 --> 00:13:05,677
thanks to the trust he built among
the beast pirates over many years.

216
00:13:05,760 --> 00:13:08,000
He quietly leads his foe into a trap.

217
00:13:09,480 --> 00:13:10,520
See, prismstone?

218
00:13:10,740 --> 00:13:11,877
What the hell are you doing?

219
00:13:11,960 --> 00:13:12,790
Get off!

220
00:13:12,873 --> 00:13:14,720
Fetch the restraints. Sir!

221
00:13:16,100 --> 00:13:18,800
This some kind of joke? Release me!

222
00:13:19,240 --> 00:13:21,740
Bind his mouth, too. Yes, sir!

223
00:13:22,200 --> 00:13:23,880
Kyoshiro, answer me!

224
00:13:24,140 --> 00:13:25,680
Calm down, Sasaki.

225
00:13:26,100 --> 00:13:29,920
Tell me, what do you know about
the land of Wano's history?

226
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:32,560
Huh? That tattoo!

227
00:13:37,920 --> 00:13:41,157
After effortlessly besting
one of the fearsome Tobiroko,

228
00:13:41,240 --> 00:13:45,380
Denjiro splits his group into two
just as the eastern forces did.

229
00:13:45,640 --> 00:13:47,637
You can enter the dome from there.

230
00:13:47,720 --> 00:13:48,896
Best of luck to you.

231
00:13:50,460 --> 00:13:56,100
The ambush on Kaido draws ever closer as
the southern forces steadily close in.

232
00:14:06,360 --> 00:14:07,190
No!

233
00:14:14,460 --> 00:14:16,957
We're not through! Come here!

234
00:14:17,040 --> 00:14:18,746
I knew that it wouldn't play!

235
00:14:19,060 --> 00:14:20,001
We're gonna die!

236
00:14:20,260 --> 00:14:21,340
Oh, raccoon!

237
00:14:21,760 --> 00:14:22,860
Time to die!

238
00:14:25,900 --> 00:14:27,440
They distracted her.

239
00:14:27,620 --> 00:14:28,796
I hope they're safe.

240
00:14:29,060 --> 00:14:30,400
Fierce and mature.

241
00:14:34,020 --> 00:14:35,820
How admirable of them both.

242
00:14:36,040 --> 00:14:38,477
Even fleeing in terror,
they lured her away.

243
00:14:38,560 --> 00:14:39,678
We're in your debt.

244
00:14:39,800 --> 00:14:41,506
Thank you, Commander Chopper.

245
00:14:41,900 --> 00:14:45,200
And you, Driver Uzzah,
let us march forth, sir!

246
00:14:46,020 --> 00:14:46,850
Onward, men!

247
00:14:47,020 --> 00:14:49,837
We must not let their honorable
sacrifice go to waste!

248
00:14:49,920 --> 00:14:51,837
Maybe we should stop and assist them.

249
00:14:51,920 --> 00:14:54,037
They surely need our
help with that monster.

250
00:14:54,120 --> 00:14:57,117
What if she's too much woman
for those boys to handle?

251
00:14:57,200 --> 00:14:58,141
She has a point!

252
00:14:58,320 --> 00:14:59,280
It is Big Mom!

253
00:14:59,420 --> 00:15:00,697
Then help how exactly?

254
00:15:00,780 --> 00:15:02,577
I don't think there's anything we can do.

255
00:15:02,660 --> 00:15:05,877
We'll have to thank them for the
diversion when they get back.

256
00:15:05,960 --> 00:15:07,800
Jeez, why is it so hot in here?

257
00:15:09,440 --> 00:15:11,720
Nabi, I love you! We've got trouble!

258
00:15:14,540 --> 00:15:15,880
Finally found you!

259
00:15:16,860 --> 00:15:17,780
Hey, Mama!

260
00:15:17,980 --> 00:15:20,745
The lady who kidnapped
Zeus is right over here!

261
00:15:22,540 --> 00:15:24,520
That's the leg! Papa!

262
00:15:24,820 --> 00:15:26,740
That's the leg! Papa!

263
00:15:27,260 --> 00:15:29,917
Can't you do that down a
different hallway, you idiot?

264
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:31,353
What was that, Papa?

265
00:15:31,500 --> 00:15:35,480
How about you say that to my
cute little face? Just shut up!

266
00:15:37,060 --> 00:15:38,780
I'm ever so tired!

267
00:15:39,080 --> 00:15:40,240
How heartless!

268
00:15:40,580 --> 00:15:43,180
Would you treat me like
this if I was dying?

269
00:15:43,760 --> 00:15:45,700
Poor little oldie!

270
00:15:46,400 --> 00:15:47,640
Don't be like that.

271
00:15:47,880 --> 00:15:49,897
If you're so tired, just sit there.

272
00:15:49,980 --> 00:15:52,274
That's not what you're supposed to say!

273
00:15:53,640 --> 00:15:54,520
Oh crap!

274
00:15:55,520 --> 00:15:58,857
This is the part where you offer
to give me a piggyback ride!

275
00:15:58,940 --> 00:16:02,580
Hey, you're choking, wait! Stop!

276
00:16:02,960 --> 00:16:04,240
Ease your grip, sis!

277
00:16:04,480 --> 00:16:06,100
Say you're sorry!

278
00:16:06,520 --> 00:16:09,220
Come on, stop messing around!

279
00:16:12,080 --> 00:16:13,117
Papa!

280
00:16:13,200 --> 00:16:14,780
Papa!

281
00:16:14,880 --> 00:16:16,040
Papa!

282
00:16:16,140 --> 00:16:18,520
You gotta stay with me, dammit!

283
00:16:19,280 --> 00:16:22,200
Oh, my poor sweet little Papa!

284
00:16:22,340 --> 00:16:23,240
Oh, no!

285
00:16:30,440 --> 00:16:33,180
Oh, here lies Papa.

286
00:16:33,380 --> 00:16:37,140
He sacrificed his life for his
favorite person in the world.

287
00:16:39,660 --> 00:16:40,490
Huh?

288
00:16:40,573 --> 00:16:42,262
Can't you see I'm grieving here?

289
00:16:42,880 --> 00:16:44,115
Who the heck are you?

290
00:16:56,620 --> 00:16:58,880
That has to be only Gashima.

291
00:17:01,240 --> 00:17:02,400
Curse you, King.

292
00:17:03,780 --> 00:17:04,740
Mock, too.

293
00:17:06,240 --> 00:17:07,840
And that damn Straw Hat.

294
00:17:08,760 --> 00:17:10,360
Mama's Alliance be damned.

295
00:17:10,760 --> 00:17:13,584
I'm going to wreak havoc
as soon as I get there.

296
00:17:14,340 --> 00:17:18,840
Anyone who dares to cross us will
get the worst licking of their lives.

297
00:17:20,740 --> 00:17:21,680
Wait a second.

298
00:17:22,760 --> 00:17:23,819
There's a problem.

299
00:17:24,160 --> 00:17:27,217
I'm pretty sure Big Mom was
headed towards Nami's group.

300
00:17:27,300 --> 00:17:29,829
She's probably gonna
try to take back Zeus.

301
00:17:30,040 --> 00:17:31,922
So that means they're in danger.

302
00:17:32,140 --> 00:17:33,477
The damage we just took.

303
00:17:33,560 --> 00:17:36,577
I think it accidentally activated
the transformation switch.

304
00:17:36,660 --> 00:17:38,719
Don't worry, they're gonna be fine.

305
00:17:38,880 --> 00:17:40,377
Sanji's with them, remember?

306
00:17:40,460 --> 00:17:41,657
I guess you're right.

307
00:17:41,740 --> 00:17:44,757
Although I hope he doesn't
get distracted by the

308
00:17:44,840 --> 00:17:47,722
Pleasure Hall and can
focus on saving Momonosuke.

309
00:17:47,900 --> 00:17:50,312
That is the risk with him, unfortunately.

310
00:17:50,960 --> 00:17:52,666
Let's just hope for the best.

311
00:17:53,200 --> 00:17:54,030
Alright.

312
00:17:54,520 --> 00:17:59,402
At least Kinemon's group can keep moving
forward thanks to us, so that's something.

313
00:18:00,400 --> 00:18:02,576
Glad we showed them the Brachio tank.

314
00:18:02,760 --> 00:18:04,637
Bet they thought it was real cool.

315
00:18:04,720 --> 00:18:05,550
Heck yeah!

316
00:18:05,680 --> 00:18:09,877
Between Commander Chopper,
Sniper-slash-Driver Usopp, and our tank!

317
00:18:09,960 --> 00:18:12,240
Those Samurai must be in awe!

318
00:18:12,620 --> 00:18:14,032
Nothing can stop us now!

319
00:18:20,960 --> 00:18:23,080
Ma-ma-ma-ma!

320
00:18:23,720 --> 00:18:25,620
Follow me, everyone!

321
00:18:29,560 --> 00:18:32,260
Come here, little umbrella!

322
00:18:33,480 --> 00:18:35,980
You too, old Chew!

323
00:18:36,200 --> 00:18:37,540
Hurry along now!

324
00:18:40,960 --> 00:18:44,400
I want you too, Dirtwall. Yes!

325
00:18:45,060 --> 00:18:46,920
And you, Captain!

326
00:18:51,980 --> 00:18:52,860
Lantern!

327
00:18:56,880 --> 00:19:00,580
Join me and I'll give you all life!

328
00:19:02,260 --> 00:19:04,980
Come along now, little homies.

329
00:19:06,400 --> 00:19:08,837
Mama! Look! Right here!

330
00:19:08,920 --> 00:19:10,380
Knock it off!

331
00:19:10,760 --> 00:19:13,172
Stop drawing attention to us, stupid son!

332
00:19:14,360 --> 00:19:15,920
We gotta do something.

333
00:19:16,220 --> 00:19:19,867
If Mama steals me back, then
I'll be as good as dead for sure.

334
00:19:21,100 --> 00:19:24,806
Is that overripe, mature woman
really as dangerous as they say?

335
00:19:25,080 --> 00:19:27,668
She's all that and then
some, I promise you.

336
00:19:28,140 --> 00:19:28,980
Hold on.

337
00:19:29,320 --> 00:19:31,780
Wasn't Sanji supposed to be here with us?

338
00:19:33,500 --> 00:19:35,360
Yeah, I think.

339
00:19:36,140 --> 00:19:37,760
Sorry for making you worry.

340
00:19:38,140 --> 00:19:40,980
I'll find those lovely
ladies no matter what.

341
00:19:43,200 --> 00:19:44,920
Dependable as ever, I guess.

342
00:19:45,800 --> 00:19:47,240
We'll just have to run.

343
00:19:47,420 --> 00:19:50,361
We still have a mission
to rescue Lord Momonosuke.

344
00:19:52,860 --> 00:19:53,690
Hey!

345
00:19:57,200 --> 00:19:58,880
Hey! Mama!

346
00:19:59,220 --> 00:20:00,340
Over this way!

347
00:20:01,800 --> 00:20:03,537
Ma-ma-ma-ma!

348
00:20:03,620 --> 00:20:05,520
There's no need to rush.

349
00:20:05,760 --> 00:20:08,289
The performance floor
is up ahead, correct?

350
00:20:08,480 --> 00:20:10,820
They'll be right where we want them.

351
00:20:19,840 --> 00:20:23,220
I'm seeing people with weird
abilities everywhere I go.

352
00:20:24,780 --> 00:20:26,880
Just call us gifters.

353
00:20:29,940 --> 00:20:33,100
We all at one time
shared that same desire.

354
00:20:33,620 --> 00:20:38,877
Every one of us things will be so
much easier for you if you defect.

355
00:20:38,960 --> 00:20:41,760
There's nearly 500 of us.

356
00:20:42,340 --> 00:20:45,477
It ain't so bad—have
a fresh start with us.

357
00:20:45,560 --> 00:20:46,390
Kid,

358
00:20:48,100 --> 00:20:50,377
you sure you still want
to take them head on?

359
00:20:50,460 --> 00:20:56,017
Sneaking in would be easier; we've already
lost a bunch of crewmates to the chaos.

360
00:20:56,100 --> 00:20:59,197
I'm sure they can make it through
on their own, but we gotta.

361
00:20:59,280 --> 00:21:01,537
gotta We're gonna stick
together till we meet up again.

362
00:21:01,620 --> 00:21:04,180
If I kill you, I'll get promoted for sure.

363
00:21:04,560 --> 00:21:06,220
Nothing personal, of course.

364
00:21:10,740 --> 00:21:11,800
Please stop!

365
00:21:12,080 --> 00:21:13,797
The commander is looking for you!

366
00:21:13,880 --> 00:21:15,409
Leave me alone, all right?

367
00:21:15,560 --> 00:21:17,240
I've got places to be!

368
00:21:17,540 --> 00:21:19,260
Master, please wait!

369
00:21:19,960 --> 00:21:23,400
If you let your guard down,
you might get yourself killed!

370
00:21:30,720 --> 00:21:31,837
Oh baby!

371
00:21:31,920 --> 00:21:34,860
My poor sweet little baby brother!

372
00:21:35,260 --> 00:21:36,680
Did you get a boo-boo?

373
00:21:36,980 --> 00:21:40,100
I'm ever, ever so happy that you're okay!

374
00:21:42,400 --> 00:21:44,120
What are you looking at?

375
00:21:45,040 --> 00:21:46,500
How dare you!

376
00:21:46,980 --> 00:21:49,437
Whom do you think you are
hurting him like that?

377
00:21:49,520 --> 00:21:51,200
You're out of line, pal.

378
00:21:51,480 --> 00:21:54,120
Only I'm allowed to bully Papa.

379
00:21:55,920 --> 00:21:56,750
Huh?

380
00:21:58,500 --> 00:22:01,097
You were the one surfing
on him down the stairs.

381
00:22:01,180 --> 00:22:02,298
I didn't touch him.

382
00:22:03,500 --> 00:22:04,800
Who are you?

383
00:22:04,980 --> 00:22:06,460
What unit are you with?

384
00:22:06,580 --> 00:22:08,257
Who's your commanding officer?

385
00:22:08,340 --> 00:22:11,120
I don't think he's one of ours. Huh? What?

386
00:22:11,320 --> 00:22:12,700
He's an intruder.

387
00:22:13,640 --> 00:22:14,700
The Nerve.

388
00:22:15,180 --> 00:22:16,600
The name's Luffy.

389
00:22:17,240 --> 00:22:19,946
The man who's going to
be king of the pirates.

390
00:22:29,500 --> 00:22:30,620
Excuse you?

391
00:22:30,860 --> 00:22:31,980
Oh, boy.

392
00:22:32,340 --> 00:22:36,105
Do you have the teeniest clue
whose mansion you stepped foot in?

393
00:22:36,620 --> 00:22:37,450
Newsflash!

394
00:22:37,533 --> 00:22:42,200
It belongs to Commander Kaido, who's
going to be the real king of the pirates!

395
00:22:44,140 --> 00:22:46,375
You're the dumbest dummy in the world!

396
00:22:47,520 --> 00:22:50,820
I'm going to fully drive stallion, too!

397
00:22:52,580 --> 00:22:53,740
Headfoot!

398
00:22:55,740 --> 00:22:56,900
Ultimoder!

399
00:23:28,280 --> 00:23:31,120
Hey, sis, be careful of him, all right?

400
00:23:31,520 --> 00:23:32,760
Yeah, I got it.

401
00:23:39,200 --> 00:23:41,960
Wanna help, Papa? Sure.

402
00:24:11,200 --> 00:24:13,980
Excuse me, is all this really necessary?

403
00:24:14,780 --> 00:24:18,251
Harry, why would you resort to
transforming when he's down?

404
00:24:19,660 --> 00:24:20,680
Lady Ulti?

405
00:24:24,480 --> 00:24:25,680
Page one, sir?

406
00:24:28,780 --> 00:24:30,080
Maybe I'm out of line.

407
00:24:30,360 --> 00:24:31,317
This seems excessive.

408
00:24:31,400 --> 00:24:32,635
Shut your damn mouth!

409
00:24:33,820 --> 00:24:36,140
I can make up my own mind.

410
00:24:36,580 --> 00:24:40,500
And we already decided that
this guy's a dangerous enemy.

411
00:24:40,800 --> 00:24:41,657
I don't know, ma 'am.

412
00:24:41,740 --> 00:24:42,917
He looks pretty dead to me.

413
00:24:43,000 --> 00:24:44,824
Hey, you cracked his head open!

414
00:24:50,220 --> 00:24:53,497
Then where the hell is all
that Haki coming from, huh?

415
00:24:53,580 --> 00:24:55,880
Hot heart! Hey!

416
00:25:03,380 --> 00:25:05,500
You guys are tougher than you look.

417
00:25:05,940 --> 00:25:07,340
Didn't see that coming.

418
00:25:09,120 --> 00:25:11,180
Guess I underestimated you.

419
00:25:12,200 --> 00:25:14,000
It won't happen again.

420
00:25:16,080 --> 00:25:19,000
This is an emperor's home turf after all.

421
00:25:21,900 --> 00:25:24,517
Listen up shitheads!

422
00:25:24,600 --> 00:25:27,557
Sorry to interrupt your
scheduled drinking.

423
00:25:27,640 --> 00:25:31,220
But Shogun Orochi has a
special event for you.

424
00:25:33,440 --> 00:25:34,270
Hello.

425
00:25:34,353 --> 00:25:35,437
Testing.

426
00:25:35,520 --> 00:25:36,980
Is this thing on?

427
00:25:37,520 --> 00:25:38,350
Good.

428
00:25:38,433 --> 00:25:39,277
Welcome all.

429
00:25:39,360 --> 00:25:42,260
I come to you this
evening with a real treat.

430
00:25:46,120 --> 00:25:48,500
Does anyone recognize this boy?

431
00:25:49,040 --> 00:25:51,420
You're looking at Kozuki Oden's son.

432
00:25:51,680 --> 00:25:53,974
He was thought to be dead 20 years ago.

433
00:25:57,260 --> 00:25:59,060
Now come, come!

434
00:26:16,260 --> 00:26:18,220
Fix this!

435
00:26:34,360 --> 00:26:35,480
Drop them!

436
00:26:40,320 --> 00:26:41,760
OLEPHANT GUNS!!!

437
00:26:46,460 --> 00:26:48,800
Are you okay? That looked bad!

438
00:26:49,200 --> 00:26:50,280
Page one, sir!

439
00:26:53,380 --> 00:26:55,880
Listen here, you slimeball!

440
00:26:56,320 --> 00:26:59,440
You've got some nerve-hurting Papa!

441
00:27:06,320 --> 00:27:08,400
I'm gonna crush you!

442
00:27:08,840 --> 00:27:11,077
Lady Olsen pulled out her dinosaur board!

443
00:27:11,160 --> 00:27:13,397
Please, this place can't
take this kind of damage!

444
00:27:13,480 --> 00:27:14,310
Stop!

445
00:27:14,393 --> 00:27:15,900
That's a good grip!

446
00:27:16,340 --> 00:27:17,700
She's really strong!

447
00:27:20,640 --> 00:27:22,000
Naughty Meteor!

448
00:27:25,820 --> 00:27:26,650
Crap!

449
00:27:27,020 --> 00:27:28,700
What? Deer!

450
00:27:35,600 --> 00:27:37,000
Ahhhhh!

451
00:27:40,000 --> 00:27:40,830
Thunder!

452
00:27:40,913 --> 00:27:41,743
Aqua!

453
00:28:05,480 --> 00:28:06,310
Nooo!

454
00:28:51,300 --> 00:28:53,120
Straw Hat Luffy

455
00:28:56,860 --> 00:28:58,920
It's really you, isn't it?

456
00:29:03,940 --> 00:29:05,120
Uh, yeah?

457
00:29:18,700 --> 00:29:20,277
They're getting away!

458
00:29:20,360 --> 00:29:21,595
They're getting away!

459
00:29:22,200 --> 00:29:23,040
Seize them!

460
00:29:30,020 --> 00:29:31,120
Forgive me.

461
00:29:31,360 --> 00:29:33,280
I swear I mean you no harm.

462
00:29:38,280 --> 00:29:39,110
Alright.

463
00:29:39,193 --> 00:29:41,840
You seem like a good person. Put me down.

464
00:29:42,460 --> 00:29:43,290
You hear me?

465
00:29:43,440 --> 00:29:45,146
There's something I gotta do.

466
00:29:45,380 --> 00:29:47,660
The day has finally come.

467
00:29:49,560 --> 00:29:56,260
Now, I understand this may sound odd, but
I've anticipated this for quite some time.

468
00:29:57,700 --> 00:29:59,640
I've been waiting for you.

469
00:30:07,480 --> 00:30:09,940
My name is Yamato.

470
00:30:10,400 --> 00:30:12,660
I'm Kaido's son!
